{"1-3":{"people":[{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":1}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H8356","lemma":"שָׁת","tr":"sha·tah","gloss":"foundation","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H0652","lemma":"אֹ֫פֶל","tr":"o·phel","gloss":"darkness","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"H1119","lemma":"בְּמוֹ","tr":"be·mo","gloss":"in","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"H5110","lemma":"נוּד","tr":"nud","gloss":"to wander","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":24},{"base":"H2620","lemma":"חָסָה","tr":"cha·sah","gloss":"to seek refuge","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":37},{"base":"H6833","lemma":"צִפּוֹר","tr":"tsip·por","gloss":"bird","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":40},{"base":"H2040","lemma":"הָרַס","tr":"ha·ras","gloss":"to overthrow","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":43},{"base":"H2671","lemma":"חֵץ","tr":"chets","gloss":"arrow","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":53},{"base":"H6466","lemma":"פָּעַל","tr":"pa·al","gloss":"to work","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":57},{"base":"H1869","lemma":"דָּרַךְ","tr":"da·rakh","gloss":"to tread","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":62}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":82,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":27,"source":"both","text":"They do not know or understand; they wander in the darkness; all the foundations of the earth are shaken.","from":3},{"book":"2TI","chapter":2,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":19,"source":"both","text":"Nevertheless, Godʼs firm foundation stands, bearing this seal: “The Lord knows those who are His,” and, “Everyone who calls on the name of the Lord must turn away from iniquity.”","from":3},{"book":"ISA","chapter":58,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":18,"source":"both","text":"Your people will rebuild the ancient ruins; you will restore the age-old foundations; you will be called Repairer of the Breach, Restorer of the Streets of Dwelling.","from":3},{"book":"PSA","chapter":56,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"in God I trust; I will not be afraid. What can man do to me?","from":1},{"book":"ISA","chapter":26,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"You will keep in perfect peace the steadfast of mind, because he trusts in You.","from":1},{"book":"ISA","chapter":26,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"Trust in the LORD forever, because GOD the LORD is the Rock eternal.","from":1},{"book":"1SA","chapter":23,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"And David stayed in the wilderness strongholds and in the hill country of the Wilderness of Ziph. Day after day Saul searched for him, but God would not deliver David into his hand.","from":1},{"book":"PSA","chapter":25,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"in You, my God, I trust. Do not let me be put to shame; do not let my enemies exult over me.","from":1}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"4-7":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H0974","lemma":"בָּחַן","tr":"ba·chan","gloss":"to test","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":29},{"base":"H2372","lemma":"חָזָה","tr":"cha·zah","gloss":"to see","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":55},{"base":"H6662","lemma":"צַדִּיק","tr":"tsad·diq","gloss":"righteous","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":206},{"base":"H0157","lemma":"אָהֵב","tr":"a·hav","gloss":"to love: lover","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":211},{"base":"H7563","lemma":"רָשָׁע","tr":"ra·sah","gloss":"wicked","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":263},{"base":"H2152","lemma":"זַלְעָפָה","tr":"zal·a·phah","gloss":"scorching","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H1614","lemma":"גׇּפְרִית","tr":"goph·rit","gloss":"brimstone","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H4521","lemma":"מְנָת","tr":"me·nat","gloss":"portion","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H6079","lemma":"עַפְעַף","tr":"aph·aph","gloss":"eyelid","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"H4305","lemma":"מָטַר","tr":"ma·tar","gloss":"to rain","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":17}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":103,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"The LORD has established His throne in heaven, and His kingdom rules over all.","from":4},{"book":"REV","chapter":22,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":13,"source":"openbible","text":"They will see His face, and His name will be on their foreheads.","from":7},{"book":"PSA","chapter":17,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":12,"source":"openbible","text":"As for me, I will behold Your face in righteousness; when I awake, I will be satisfied in Your presence.","from":7},{"book":"GEN","chapter":19,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Then the Lordrained down sulfur and fire on Sodom and Gomorrah—from the Lordout of the heavens.","from":6},{"book":"PSA","chapter":2,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"The One enthroned in heaven laughs; the Lord taunts them.","from":4},{"book":"PSA","chapter":18,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"In my distress I called upon the LORD; I cried to my God for help. From His temple He heard my voice, and my cry for His help reached His ears.","from":4},{"book":"PRO","chapter":6,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"There are six things that the LORD hates, seven that are detestable to Him:","from":5},{"book":"PRO","chapter":6,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"a false witness who gives false testimony, and one who stirs up discord among brothers.","from":5}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}